cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it as below."
title: "SET v1.8: a machine-checked mathematical framework with two registered, falsifiable predictions"
authors:
  - family-names: "Shepherd"
    given-names: "Corey"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Olive Hill, Kentucky, USA"
version: "1.8"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21927298
date-released: "2026-08-13"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A body of mathematical work built from a single postulated object, the
  horn torus, whose radial metric is the Fisher information metric of a
  Bernoulli variable, plus one experimental calibrant and an explicitly
  listed assumption ledger. The record derives a large set of physical
  quantities (labeled postdictions), a dark-matter candidate (chain 31,
  CANDIDATE, resting on the named postulate P-RING and the conditional
  Q-LAW), and two registered predictions with explicit kill conditions:
  P6 (dark-matter-to-baryon ratio exactly 2pi - 1, CANDIDATE carrier on
  proven internal geometry) and P7 (eternal direct-detection null). All
  claims labeled PROVEN carry machine checks; the verification suite runs
  94 checks with zero failures at issue. Code MIT, documents CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - horn torus
  - Fisher information geometry
  - information geometry
  - Dirac operator
  - spectral geometry
  - dark matter candidate
  - falsifiable predictions
  - pre-registration
  - reproducible research
  - machine-checked mathematics
